    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0428" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1951v05/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.74/9–2751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d163-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-27T20:00:00+02:00">September 27,
                            1951—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>375. Deptel 423, Sept 24.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d163-f2"/> Minister Foreign
                    Affairs after recounting at some length reasons why Egyptian Govt must go ahead
                    at once with abrogation 1936 treaty and referring to local press attacks on
                    alleged Anglo-American plans for East Mediterranean finally agreed that he wld
                    endeavor to hold off for say ten days.</p>
                <p>Minister Foreign Affairs observed he cordially welcomed our hospitable interest
                    in this question. He said he wld at once inform Prime Minister of this. If I had
                    taken this matter up with Prime Minister rather than Foreign Minister I wld have
                    recd from Prime Minister various declarations of good will but nothing else. He
                    wld have taken no decision on this without consulting his Minister Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested Caffery to seek an early opportunity to speak to Prime
                    Minister Nahas Pasha and/or Foreign Minister Salaheddin in order to express the
                    hope that no precipitate action would be taken by the Egyptian Government “which
                    wld make difficult calm and considered deliberation new proposals” regarding the
                    MEC (641.74/9–2351).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
